// Story event-chain gRPC contract (satelle-server sty_8cd87197; the CLI half is
// satelle sty_9bdf08c4).
//
// Service Chain stores each story as an append-only chain of events. A client
// appends a story's new events together with the base event it last saw; the
// server accepts them only when that base is still the story's latest event
// (compare-and-append) and otherwise refuses with FAILED_PRECONDITION carrying a
// StaleBase detail. There are no holds, locks or checkouts on this service.
//
// The server checks only the envelope: an event is well formed, belongs to the
// story and builds on the latest. It never interprets a payload, a workflow or a
// status. The payload is the opaque CLI JSON object, like the record fields of
// satelle.sync.v1.
//
// Chain is a separate package from satelle.sync.v1 so the CLI and the server
// release independently; Sync's Apply and Snapshot are unchanged. Every RPC
// requires a bearer, refuses agent tokens, and fences the project like Sync.

